WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.944 --> 00:00:03.776
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:05.298 --> 00:00:06.840
SPEAKER: Give me
one minute, and I'll

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.970
tell you how Cloud Data
Loss Prevention can

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:11.190
help you detect and
protect sensitive data

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:13.350
across your systems.

00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:16.260
Cloud Data Loss
Prevention, or Cloud DLP,

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:19.230
is a fully managed service that
lets you discover, classify,

00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:21.330
and protect all kinds
of sensitive data

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:23.550
from various sources.

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:27.180
Cloud DLP can recognize
up to 150 different data

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:31.440
types like names, addresses,
dates, credit card, numbers

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:33.250
and more.

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:35.700
You can even define your
own custom info types

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:37.770
based on custom
dictionary detectors

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:39.840
or regular expressions.

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:42.030
Every sensitive
value that DLP finds

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:44.040
is assigned a certainty
score, ranging

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:46.980
from very unlikely
to very likely,

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:49.260
giving you the flexibility
to set a confidence

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:53.250
threshold for inspections
and de-identification jobs.

00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:56.700
Speaking of de-identification,
the Cloud DLP API

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:59.040
offers a number of
de-identification techniques

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:02.340
to obscure, mask,
tokenize, or transform

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.459
those sensitive values in
your data based on the info

00:01:05.459 --> 00:01:07.710
type and the likelihood score.

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:10.140
With Cloud DLP, you
can send data directly

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:12.420
into the API or
schedule inspection

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:13.980
jobs that will scan
the data that you

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:15.820
specify for sensitive values.

00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:18.120
So you can regularly gain
visibility into the data

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:20.250
that you store and process.

00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:23.250
Cloud DLP has built-in support
for scanning and classifying

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:25.890
data from Cloud
Storage and BigQuery

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:28.950
and has a streaming
content API and hybrid

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:31.440
API so that you can
scan other data sources,

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:34.020
or so you can use it as
part of custom workloads

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:35.610
and applications.

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:38.640
The API even leverages
optical character recognition

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:40.720
to scan images for
sensitive data,

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:42.360
allowing you to
detect and redact

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:44.460
that data from image files.

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:47.160
So next time you're looking to
detect, classify, and secure

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:49.830
your sensitive data, take a
minute to look at Cloud Data

00:01:49.830 --> 00:01:50.880
Loss Prevention.

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:54.680
To learn more check out
cloud.google.com/dlp.

